      "heading": "Davao comparisons",
      "id": "P004",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "Prosecution counsel Rep. Jonathan Keith T. Flores emphasized the six-million-peso deed consideration against the ten-million-peso SALN acquisition cost. Defense counsel Attorney Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel relied on the matching assessed value and argued that Matina Crossing was Barangay 74-A. He also elicited roughly 8.8 million pesos in combined land and building market values, plus additional fees. Those were different figures from the deed price and the assessed value. Presiding Officer Sen. Francis \"Chiz\" G. Escudero requested assessor mapping and supporting material before deciding the defense request for judicial notice. Baldonado said the registry did not hold SALNs and she lacked personal knowledge of their completeness."
    },
