      "heading": "Court directions and witness planning",
      "id": "P008",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "The chair allowed the registry testimony over defense relevance and notice objections and directed circulation and later exhibit marking of the records. He allowed confrontation with newer tax declarations on cross-examination, subject to witness knowledge, limiting Baldonado's answers to their contents rather than their truth. Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo urged a more useful witness sequence and proposed hearing Sonny Trillanes before the Anti-Money Laundering Council, or AMLC. The chair left that choice to the prosecution. Rep. Gerville R. Luistro later withdrew Trillanes from its witness list."
    },
