      "heading": "AMLC confidentiality and preparation",
      "id": "P009",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "Before the planned AMLC examination, lead defense counsel Attorney Sheila C. Sison sought time to compare summaries and annexes with 23 to 24 boxes of material and prepare objections and questions. She argued that the material remained confidential and that the July subpoena ruling reserved later objections. Prosecution counsel Rep. Jose Manuel \"Chel\" I. Diokno opposed delay, saying the underlying documents had been furnished September 2. He distinguished unauthorized disclosure from lawful subpoena compliance and urged examination with objections addressed as they arose. Sen. Risa Hontiveros similarly argued that confidentiality barred indiscriminate leaks rather than lawful court disclosure."
    },
