      "heading": "Preparation granted; Monday resumption",
      "id": "P010",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III expressed strong reservations about postponement. Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano supported preparation until Monday, balancing speed with fairness after the summaries arrived that morning. Sen. Francis Pangilinan said the AMLC issue had already been argued in July but supported a one-trial-day delay. Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson asked colleagues to study the bank-secrecy law's impeachment exception. Escudero granted defense preparation time and circulated AMLC confidentiality provisions for senator-judges to consider, with questions to be settled Monday. The revised sequence was AMLC, then banks and insurance companies, then the Bureau of Internal Revenue. Trial adjourned until Monday, October 5, at ten in the morning, with no Friday sitting."
    },
